ment commands.\",\"level\":1},{\"title\":\"Practical Example: Running 'hello-world'\",\"description\":\"Step-by-step instructions to run the classic 'hello-world' container.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Managing Running Containers\",\"description\":\"Commands to list, stop, and remove Docker containers.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Building Custom Docker Images with Dockerfile\",\"description\":\"Learn how to create your own Docker images using a Dockerfile, with a simple web application example.\",\"level\":1},{\"title\":\"Dockerfile Basics: FROM, RUN, COPY, CMD\",\"description\":\"Detailed explanation and usage of essential Dockerfile instructions.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Practical Example: Dockerizing a Simple Web App\",\"description\":\"Walkthrough of creating a Dockerfile for a basic Node.js or Python web application.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Tagging and Pushing Images to Docker Hub\",\"description\":\"How to tag your custom images and share them with the world via Docker Hub.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Advanced Container Management\",\"description\":\"Commands for inspecting container details, executing commands inside a running container, and viewing logs.\",\"level\":1},{\"title\":\"Inspecting Container Details\",\"description\":\"Using `docker inspect` to get detailed information about a container.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Executing Commands Inside a Container\",\"description\":\"How to use `docker exec` to interact with a running container.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Viewing Container Logs\",\"description\":\"Understanding and using `docker logs` to troubleshoot and monitor containers.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Data Persistence with Docker Volumes\",\"description\":\"Understanding why data persistence is crucial and how Docker Volumes provide it.\",\"level\":1},{\"title\":\"Practical Example: Using Named Volumes\",\"description\":\"Demonstration of creating and attaching named volumes to containers for persistent data storage.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Container Communication with Docker Networks\",\"description\":\"An introduction to Docker networking concepts and how containers communicate with each other.\",\"level\":1},{\"title\":\"Practical Example: User-Defined Bridge Networks\",\"description\":\"Setting up a custom network to allow multiple containers (e.g., web app and database) to communicate.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Orchestration for Beginners: Introduction to Docker Compose\",\"description\":\"Learn how Docker Compose simplifies the management of multi-container Docker applications.\",\"level\":1},{\"title\":\"Practical Example: A Multi-Service Application with Docker Compose\",\"description\":\"Building and running a simple web application with a database using a `docker-compose.yml` file.\",\"level\":2},{\"title\":\"Docker Best Practices for Beginners\",\"description\":\"Tips and tricks for writing efficient Dockerfiles and managing your Docker environment effectively.\",\"level\":1},{\"title\":\"Conclusion and Next Steps\",\"description\":\"Summarizing the benefits of Docker and suggesting further learning resources for continued growth.\",\"level\":1}]}","responseLength":4090,"tokenUsage":{"inputTokens":2364,"outputTokens":1268,"totalTokens":6203},"estimatedCost":0.001115,"promptName":"planner","promptVersion":"v1","retryCount":3}
